Third-party proprietary components in the binary releases
---------------------------------------------------------
The paragraph above is about the source repository. The **binary releases**
(the OTA package, super.img / boot.img and the installer images published on
GitHub Releases and on the update server) DO contain the following third-party
components. They are **not** covered by this project's GPL license, they are
not open source, and their copyright belongs to their respective owners
(Huawei, Qualcomm, Google). We have no license from those owners to
redistribute them. They are listed here so that anyone who mirrors or
redistributes the images knows what is inside. Plain-language summary and
consequences: section 2 of docs/known-limitations.md
("Proprietary components shipped in the images").

* Huawei firmware for this device, installed under
  /vendor/firmware/qcom/sc8280xp/HUAWEI/gaokun3/ (and copied into the boot.img
  ramdisk; the installer images carry the GPU zap shader as well):
      qcdxkmsuc8280.mbn                       GPU zap shader
      qcadsp8280.mbn, qccdsp8280.mbn,
      qcslpi8280.mbn                          ADSP / CDSP / SLPI firmware
      audioreach-tplg.bin                     audio topology (also installed a
                                              second time under another name
                                              in /vendor/firmware/qcom/sc8280xp/)
      qcvss8280.mbn                           voice services
      adspr.jsn, adspua.jsn, battmgr.jsn,
      cdspr.jsn                               pd_mapper service tables
  Source: Huawei's Windows driver packages. File list:
  device/huawei/gaokun3/firmware/README.md.
* Sensor DSP configuration served to the SLPI, installed under
  /vendor/etc/hexagonrpcd-root/ (sensor JSON configuration, the sns_reg.conf
  registry index, socinfo files and the SLPI companion blob RSCS.bin).
  Source: the same Windows driver packages (Qualcomm reference configuration).
  See device/huawei/gaokun3/hexagonrpcd-root/README.md.
* Huawei Histen audio engine, /vendor/lib64/soundfx/libhw_histen_processing.so:
  proprietary to Huawei, not licensed for redistribution, and binary-modified
  (patched so that Android's bionic linker can load it). It processes audio only
  when "Speaker enhancement (experimental)" is turned on. See
  device/huawei/gaokun3/effects/README.md and
  device/huawei/gaokun3/effects/prebuilt/README.md.
* Qualcomm QNN runtime (libQnnHtp.so, libQnnHtpV68Stub.so, libQnnSystem.so
  under /vendor/lib64/gk3denoise/, libQnnHtpV68Skel.so under
  /vendor/dsp/gk3denoise/), used only by the noise suppression service:
  Qualcomm's AI Stack License, /vendor/etc/gk3denoise/QNN-LICENSE.pdf and
  QNN-NOTICE.txt. Whoever builds the images downloads it from Qualcomm at
  build time and thereby accepts that licence; it is not part of this
  repository. See device/huawei/gaokun3/denoise/prebuilt/README.md.
* CDSP user-PD shell and its C++ runtime (fastrpc_shell_unsigned_3,
  libc++.so.1, libc++abi.so.1 under /vendor/dsp/gk3denoise/): from the same
  Windows driver packages as the firmware above.
* Google apps and services (MindTheGapps: Play Store, Play services, ...),
  under Google's own terms.

Not affected by the above: the GPU microcode (qcom/a660_sqe.fw,
qcom/a660_gmu.bin), the Wi-Fi firmware (ath11k/WCN6855/) and the Bluetooth
